  "id": "lowfield-cnp-thomas-pulse",
  "name": "Cnp Thomas pulse (patent table, 40 min)",
  "category": "lowfield",
  "evidence": "single-lab",
  "origin": "Lawson Health Research Institute / University of Western Ontario (A.W. Thomas, F.S. Prato); patent co-inventors M. Kavaliers and M.A. Persinger",
  "uT": 5,
  "summary": "The Lawson Cnp analgesia waveform, the decelerating \"Thomas pulse\", played exactly from Table 1 of US patent 6,234,953 on all eight temporal coils, in the 4-burst cycle and 40-min session of the Thomas 2007 headset trial. A pattern replica at about 60-100 times less field.",
  "notes": "The table is the patent's 1-ms point table read column-major, as the patent states: 18 identical 27-ms pulses whose spacing grows from 28 to about 67 ms, so the rate slows from about 36 to 15 pulses per second. Each cycle has four bursts with 110, 220, 330 and 1200 ms refractory pauses, with 838 ms per burst as Camera 2015 state (5212-ms cycle, about 460 cycles in 40 min). An 838-ms burst cuts the patent's last pulse 11 ms before its end; the separate \"Thomas pulse\" preset keeps it whole (849 ms). The sources do not say which waveform version the Thomas 2007 headset played. All eight temporal coils run in phase, left and right identical, standing in for the bilateral headset worn just above the ears. Thomas 2007 report 400 µT at the headset, ±200 µT at the head surface and ±35 µT deep in the brain; this helmet gives at most about 5 µT at 20 mm and 0.3-0.6 µT deep, about 60-100 times less, so this copies the timing only (Camera 2015 model the rate of change of the field as the stimulus). The authors described Thomas 2007 as essentially a negative study (fibromyalgia subgroup P = 0.06, n = 17); the human Cnp studies are small and single-lab, and the patent lists Persinger as a co-inventor, so this line is not independent of the God Helmet lab. Not a pain treatment: don't change medication or treatment. Not for people with epilepsy; stop on headache or distress.",
  "setting": "Seated or reclined in a quiet room (Thomas 2007 compared against identical, silent sham headsets).",
  "schedule": "Thomas 2007: 40 min twice a day, at least 4 h apart, for 7 days. Shupak 2004/2006: one 30-min session.",
  "targets": [
    "left-superior-temporal-gyrus-posterior",
    "right-superior-temporal-gyrus-posterior"
  ],
